  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Applied Research Associates has federal contract obligations of $320M in FY2026 to date. Applied Research Associates has won 177 awards so far this fiscal year, with an average award size of $1.8M. Obligations fell down 30.0% year over year. The Department of Defense is the largest buyer, obligating $239M in FY2026 to date, and the General Services Administration is the second largest with $62.4M. Engineering Services and Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences are the two largest markets, with $108M and $104M respectively. Historical obligations show a peak of $533M in FY23, followed by $476M in FY24 and $457M in FY25, before the current-year total of $320M. Smaller buying agencies in FY2026 to date include the Department of Homeland Security with $11.7M and the Department of the Interior with $4.1M.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Who are Applied Research Associates' biggest federal customers?",
        "body": "The Department of Defense is the largest customer, obligating $239M in FY2026 to date. The General Services Administration is the second largest buyer with $62.4M. The Department of Homeland Security and the Department of the Interior follow with $11.7M and $4.1M respectively. Other agencies with recorded FY2026 to date obligations include the Department of Transportation with $2.3M and the National Aeronautics and Space Administration with $17.5K."
      },
      {
        "heading": "What markets drive Applied Research Associates' federal work?",
        "body": "Engineering Services is the largest market with $108M in FY2026 to date. Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences is the next largest market with $104M. Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences (except Biotechnology) accounts for $64.5M, and All Other Professional, Scientific, and Technical Services accounts for $20.6M. Other markets include Research and Development in Biotechnology at $10.5M and Facilities Support Services at $4.5M."
      }
    ]
  },
